WEBVTT

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.790
Such a cute song!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:27.120
Ya hear that? That's your special new song, courtesy of me-kuma!

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.500
Yeah, it's great! I love it!

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.210
I like it too, but...

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.760
Why are you so puffed up over it-pri?

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.310
Not like you actually made the song-pri.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.530
You got any idea what you're saying-kuma?!

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.720
Lemme tell you how hard it is to get a new song-kuma!

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.920
You've gotta compete to get the good ones-kuma!

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.440
You work day and night to sell your idols to a creator,

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.530
and eventually you might be rewarded with a song that fits them just right-kuma!

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:56.420
Wow, really? A song just for us...

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.800
I can't wait to sing it!

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.800
We're rolling it out at the event two days from now-kuma.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.560
You better have the lyrics and choreography perfectly memorized by then-kuma.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.710
Capisce!

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.900
This new song'll be it-pri!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.660
We'll raise our rank tons and try to catch up to her!

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.160
Sophie...

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.370
Good work out there!

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.570
As always, you did great today, Lady Sophie!

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.780
Thank you. I'm just glad you li... li-liiiked...

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.920
Pshu.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.520
Chanko!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:41.780
Oh no!

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.040
Get her some pickled plums—Red Flash, stat!

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.000
Yes ma'am!

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.960
Gotchanko!

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.390
Lady Sophie.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.090
Right. Autograph event next? Let's be on our way.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.560
Right, Lady Sophie!

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.800
Sophie's in Debut class.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.490
We're both in the Student class.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.130
We can't even enter the same events as her.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.950
Our first step will be to increase our Idol Ranks until we reach Debut class.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.070
I see.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:51.990
Capisce!

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.510
Do you have the dance down?

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.670
Yeah, perfectly!

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.380
And I have another idea for
the announcement of our new song.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.840
We'll Step Up by making a new Making Drama to go with it!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.970
Sketchbook?

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.820
Whuh!?

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.350
Rule number 15420:

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.600
Don't mix up "Sketchbook" and "Step Up."

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.020
There's a crazy nitpicky rule like that!?

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.820
You don't let up even when you're off-duty, Head Disciplinarian.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.750
Step Up...

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:26.530
We're making a Making Drama to follow up on "Exciting Present For You" with.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.740
My calculations are perfect.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.760
Welcome to Prism Stone.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.870
Please enter your My Ticket.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.950
Popping Gala Complete! Pri!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.600
Huuuh?!

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.880
The training rooms are totally jam-packed!

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.270
Everyone's here because it's summer vacation-pri!

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.850
Packed in like sardines.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.990
Not in my calculations-pri!

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.420
Not good. We'll have to find some other place.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.770
Other place...

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.400
What about your place?

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.410
Huh?

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.630
Truly exquisite!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.170
This pizza is most excellent!

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.570
Thank yourtilla.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.970
By the way, is Lala out today?

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.140
Yes, she's out playing with a friend.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.100
Friend?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.530
How indecent!

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:38.060
All of this "playing with friends" nonsense is a complete waste of time!

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.480
Huh?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.900
Uh... I'd like some waffles for dessert.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.190
Very well.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.360
Wafflermative.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:51.980
I see. Headmistress Ookanda is a regular at your restaurant now.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.710
Unfortunately.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.080
I guess there's no other way.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.850
We'll just have to go to my place then.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.510
Huh?

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.160
Whoa, it's wonderful!

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.470
Come on in then.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.560
What must her mother be like...

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.510
What if...

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.070
She's like this?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.470
Scary!

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:13.430
Welcome!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.890
G-G-Good wafflenoon—no, I mean...

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:20.350
<i>Phew, she seems nice.</i>

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.430
This is Manaka Lala, an underclassman of mine.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.480
Pleased to meet you!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:29.820
Uh, the head—I mean, Mireille always helps me out with stuff. Pleased to meet you.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.160
Hello. Pleased to meet you as well.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.040
She brings friends over so rarely.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.500
Okay, this way.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.000
Coming!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.140
After you.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:41.960
Okay!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:46.010
Wow! Is this all manga? Nope!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.750
Woah, it's like all kanji!

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.630
You do read books too, don't you?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.600
Hmm... Ah! It's Mr. Kuma!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.800
No it's not!

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.020
See! Look carefully!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.730
Hmm... Well, when you say it like that...

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.230
<i>Real "pop."</i>

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.400
L-Let's get to work on ideas for the Making Drama!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.660
Gah, it really is full of kanji.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:15.080
Hm? Is this... a photo album!

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.720
Wow! So cute!

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.040
This is you when you were little, right?

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:25.540
You look like you're having so much fun on this merry-go-round!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.550
Lala! We didn't come here to horse around!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.420
Save that for after we work the Making Drama out.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.130
Capisce.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.070
<i>She's definitely easier to talk to when she's in idol form.</i>

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.180
Hey.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:38.850
Yeah?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.310
How did you come up with that Making Drama, anyway?

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:51.490
I wanted to say thanks to you and get that feeling across to all the fans, too.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.730
Conveying emotions through song...

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:57.330
You're right. The Making Drama is a message to our fans.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:01.040
We'll start by figuring out what we want to convey to them.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.240
Yeah.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.070
What's the most important thing we could tell our fans right now?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:07.500
Yes?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.010
I'm home, Mireille.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.170
Welcome home, Father.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.220
How about you join us for tea downstairs?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.140
But this really is a surprise.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.150
Isn't this the first time you've ever brought a friend over?

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.360
This really did come out of the blue.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.960
Will you stop harping on that?

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.820
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:35.300
I'm glad you and Mireille seem to get along so well, Lala.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.030
Yeah, me too!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.740
<i>This is pretty great.</i>

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.660
<i>Her mom and dad are both so refined and nice.</i>

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.990
<i>Lala! Please take some orders!</i>

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.630
<i>Come againestrata!</i>

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.950
<i>Totally different from my place.</i>

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.420
So your family runs an Italian style restaurant?

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:54.710
Oh, yeah!

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:58.580
That's nice, you must have good food all the time.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.350
Yeah, but it can make watching your weight hard.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.650
Uh, so what does your dad do?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:06.540
Prosecutor.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.310
Huh?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.380
And Mom's an attorney.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:16.070
Hm, I guess Anna's normal, but Prosecutor's gotta be a really rare name.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.790
Not names! Professions!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.340
Pro-fes-sions!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.830
Professions?

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.420
It's like...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.130
I haven't done anything!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.840
I'm innocent!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:36.800
No! Make no mistake, you ate my cake slice, Lala!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.690
You're not gonna squirm your way out of this one!

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:40.590
I have hard evidence.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.000
I'm not lying!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.630
Did you not just think mine looked much better than yours?

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.980
I didn't!

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:52.510
That's how a prosecutor has to bring the truth out.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:53.190
Huh?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.160
Yep.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:54.650
And on the other hand,

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.610
Lala isn't like that.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.110
This has to be a mistake.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:04.890
And just like that, an attorney defends the person being accused.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:07.540
Jobs like that exist?

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:12.530
Oh, we have some lovely cookies, and since Lala's here...

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.420
More importantly, don't we have some pudding in the refrigerator?

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:20.930
Yeah, we do. But doesn't tea go better with cookies?

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.150
Are you sure?

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.390
Wouldn't some nice cool pudding make more sense on a hot day like this?

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.380
But the cookies—

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:29.930
No, we need pudding!

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.410
Having cookies with tea is basically a rule.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.190
Not to mention it's easier to control your caloric intake with small, neatly portioned cookies.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.950
Do snacks even <i>have</i> official rules?

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:41.260
Clearly anyone and everyone would prefer to eat cool things in the summer.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.830
Cooling you down as it slides down your throat... Pudding is the dessert of choice in summer!

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.240
Objection!

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.580
Cookies are the rightful king of desserts with their overwhelming popularity and long history!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.040
I will not have you hurl insults at cookies!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.930
Allow me to rephrase for clarity.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:58.610
What we truly need <i>right now</i> is pudding!

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.260
Cookies would not sate our hunger!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.640
Objection!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.010
That is a completely arbitrary judgment!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.260
There's nothing arbitrary about it!

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.520
Huh? What? What's going on?

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.220
The court is in session!

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:24.950
Settling the case of cookies vs. pudding for the title of today's snack.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.540
Yes, your honor.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.080
Okaaay?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:42.990
It is hot in summer. Everyone knows this.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:46.030
Therefore, opting to eat refrigerated pudding is simply common sense. Anything else is nigh unthinkable.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.760
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.600
Therefore, opting to eat refrigerated pudding is simply common sense. Anything else is nigh unthinkable.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.020
Your honor!

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.100
The defense may speak.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.960
I would like to call Manaka Lala, representing women the world over, as a witness.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.070
Wha, witness?

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.540
Approved.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.740
Please step up, witness.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.310
Lala, do you like cookies?

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:05.870
Uh, yeah, I do!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.030
Between cookies and tonkotsu ramen, which would you choose right now?

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:15.170
Well, I do like ramen, but I guess I'd rather have cookies right now...

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.130
Objection! She's leading the witness!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.990
Lala, you like pudding too, don't you?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:21.570
Y-Yes...

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.820
But you prefer cookies, don't you?

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:25.090
Uh... Eh...

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.300
The prosecution will wait their turns.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.180
Your honor, what is the ruling?

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.180
We have made our cases.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.560
Ahem, well...

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.280
I rule as follows: We would like both cookies and pudding!

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:42.680
As such, we will have half portions of both.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:43.700
Eh?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.590
Ohh!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:51.570
Sorry about that Lala. Bit surprised?

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.330
W-Well, yeah...

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:59.300
Well, we meet a lot in court to argue like that too. I guess it comes naturally...

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:04.480
Every disagreement usually leads to that with us.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:05.760
And they don't stop once they start.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.330
It doesn't end until someone decides to act as a judge for them.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.730
Ah, I think I get why you're the way you are now...

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:20.390
But the arguing just deepens our bonds, doesn't it, dear?

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.190
Right you are, honey.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:23.780
Good grief.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.960
Come on, feelings!

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:33.830
What's that?

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:37.810
I thought if I just thought really hard maybe I'd convey something to you.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.420
You're a telepath?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.180
Seems we're a bit stuck.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:51.060
It'll be fine! I bet we'll come up with some good ideas as long as we don't give up!

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:54.060
You never give up, do you?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.270
This is pretty fun.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.730
Fun?

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.880
I used to just watch PriPara on TV.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:07.030
Being able to perform myself and brainstorm ideas for a show...

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.950
Oh! I found something I want to tell everyone!

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:10.950
Hm?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.100
How happy I am I can be an idol!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:17.290
I get to eat tasty stuff, and wear cute clothes!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.640
I've even finally learned some basic gymnastics!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:26.920
I've thought "I'm so happy!" before too, but right now I'm as happy as all the previous times put together!

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.980
Happiness... That's a big hint!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.440
You're sorely mistaken!

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.860
You're the one who's wrong!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:40.020
She's obviously going to be a prosecutor!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.770
No! She's clearly going to be a defense attorney!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:43.660
Prosecutor!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:44.230
Attorney!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.570
Stop that right now, both of you!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:48.940
Keep out of this!

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.630
I have everything under control!

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.200
No need to worry, I've got your back!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.130
Her strong sense of justice clearly makes her a natural prosecutor!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:01.420
She has always stood up for the underdog in all things! She's clearly most suited to be a defense attorney!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.300
I said prosecutor and I meant prosecutor!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.820
Attorney! She's definitely going to be an attorney!

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.130
Here you go!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.450
It's no use.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.400
This is the one argument I can't stop.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.640
Huh?

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:18.560
They've always been at each other's throats over whether I'll become a prosecutor or attorney.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.110
All you can do now is wait for it to die down.

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:24.270
Th-That's... But...

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.470
<i>She actually wants to become an idol.</i>

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.200
<i>Oh, I get it!</i>

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:36.160
<i>Is she keeping it a secret so they don't get disappointed?</i>

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.950
And you're always terribly inconsiderate!

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:44.140
You always leave all the doors open and lights on and you keep singing your heart out in the bathroom!

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.680
Two can play that game!

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:49.840
How about you stop ordering those diet products you always abandon after a few days all the time?

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:54.030
<i>Normally they get along so well, too...</i>

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.330
<i>I have to stop them somehow!</i>

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.140
<i>Err, um, uhh...</i>

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:00.810
<i>Oh yeah!</i>

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:08.820
That's slanderous!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.780
Stop!

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:13.950
Lala...

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.760
Don't you remember how well you actually get along?

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.130
Oh, I remember that!

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:23.790
Oh, that's so nostalgic!

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:29.120
She was really into amusement parks and could not settle down.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.760
And do you remember the big screen they had?

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:41.180
Right, there was a PriPara program with the Saints on!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.160
She couldn't peel her eyes away from that one.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:49.590
It's been ever since that that she wanted to become an idol.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:50.860
That's right!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:51.860
Huh?

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.300
So you actually know she wants to be an idol?

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.170
Yes.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.230
Of course.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:01.040
So what was that about prosecutor or lawyer?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.790
That's right!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.520
An idol who fights for justice, the first idol prosecutor!

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.210
Truly a job befitting her!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:13.720
No, she will be an ally to the weak! The idol attorney!

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:17.140
Cut it out, you two!

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.210
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:22.090
I'm just aiming to be a pop idol!

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:24.100
That's as far as I've thought!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.890
But...

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.560
It's such a waste...

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.710
You actually managed to defuse them, Lala.

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:30.700
Thanks.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:35.780
I just figured I'd remind them of something happy.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:40.010
Remembering happiness...

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.900
That fits right into my equation. This might just work!

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:50.330
Lala, I'll handle the Making Drama!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.970
Please scan the appropriate amount of My Tickets.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.500
You may also scan any Friend Tickets you have.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.810
Coord Change Start!

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.930
The Fresh Lime Coord.

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:13.570
The fresh lime green and orange will make for a show bursting with flavor!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.070
Fresh Lime!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.170
And the Fresh Orange Coord.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:25.120
A new design from the popular pop-style brand Candy Alamode.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.830
Fresh Orange! Pri!

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:35.590
Making Drama! Switch on!

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:05.720
Fresh Sweets Park!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.060
Cyalume Change!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.650
Pri!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.640
Announcing the results:

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:41.290
Come on, platform!

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:50.520
We pass! Great success!

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.390
Mireille's having a blast.

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:57.270
Yeah, as is Lala.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.280
Being an idol really is...

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.900
...what she's best at!

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.820
But I won't give up!

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.630
Nor will I!

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:05.670
She'll be an idol attorney!

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:08.280
She'll be an idol prosecutor!
She'll be an idol attorney!

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:08.290
She'll be an idol prosecutor!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.810
Lady Sophie, you're up soon.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:17.380
We need to hurry.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:19.700
Very well.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.670
We ranked up!

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:31.640
Yeah! Let's keep

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.410
doing our best!

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:09.380
Hooray! We got our first rank up!

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:12.290
We can finally be on the same stage as Sophie!

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:15.690
We'll work super hard to get on the same team!

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:16.990
Pshu...

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:19.210
Huh? The pickled plum pizza girl?

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:20.630
Why are you in PriPara?

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:23.420
Red Flash... please...

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.610
You mean a pickled plum?

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:26.540
Capisce!

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:29.580
I'll definitely find you one!

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:32.160
Next time: Seek the Red Flash...
